29 06:29:34'),(20,'Rhus Toxicodendron','Rhus-t','Poison Ivy','Anacardiaceae','Plant - Fresh leaves gathered at sunset just before flowering','Boericke Materia Medica, p.558-563; Allen\'s Keynotes, p.248-252','Tincture of fresh leaves gathered at sunset before flowering','Extreme restlessness, must constantly move, stiffness better by motion, worse initial motion [Boericke] skin, rheumatic pains, mucous membrane affections, and a typhoid type of fever, make this remedy frequently indicated. Rhus affects fibrous tissue markedly-joints, tendons, sheaths-aponeurosis, etc, producing pains and stiffness. Post-operative complications. Tearing asunder pains. Motion 460 always \"limbers up\" the Rhus patient, and hence he feels better for a time from a change of position. Ailments from strains, overlifting, getting wet while perspiring. Septic conditions. Cellulitis and infections, carbuncles in early stages (Echinac). Rheumatism in the cold season. Septicæmia. [Boericke] severe.','Rheumatism, sprains, herpes, restless legs, skin eruptions',NULL,'Restless, anxious, sad, weeping without cause, suicidal thoughts',' [Boericke] Vertigo when rising. Heavy head. Brain feels loose and as if struck against skull on walking or rising. Scalp sensitive; worse on side lain on. Headache in occiput (Rhus rad); painful to touch. Pain in forehead and proceeds thence backward. Humid eruptions on scalp; itching greatly.',' [Boericke] Circumscribed corneal injection. Intensive ulceration of the cornea. Iritis, after exposure to cold and dampness, and of rheumatic origin. Eye painful on turning it or pressing, can hardly move it, as in acute retrobulbar neuritis. Profuse gush of hot, scalding tears upon opening lids. [Boericke] nearly closed with great swelling. Vesicular inflammation of',' [Boericke] upon opening lids. Ears.––Pain in ears, with sensation as if something were in them. Lobules swollen. Discharge of bloody pus. [Boericke] Nose red and shiny. Face swollen. Tongue.––Red at tip. Fis